# Lesson 10 — kept boxes vs borrowed boxes
#
# Two kinds of boxes in Boxy:
#
#   make a box   = a kept box. You don't have to clean it up.
#   borrow a box = a borrowed box. You MUST return it when done.
#
# This is the most important idea in Boxy.

make a box called age
put 7 in age
say "age is ", age

borrow a box called score
put 100 in score
say "score is ", score

# Always give back what you borrow:
return score

# Try this: comment out the 'return' line above, run the lesson again,
# and read what Boxy says at the end. It will tell you which borrowed
# box you forgot, and on which line you borrowed it.
